{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And now.</b> Since I know how great is Your goodness and Your kindness toward us — that You made us a nation worthy to inherit a land, and brought us out from Egypt so that we might receive a gift that would be our own, and You have given us this one, which is the glory of all lands and the choicest of places." "<b>Behold, I have brought the first of the fruit of the ground which You have given me, HaShem.</b> I have brought the choicest fruits of that land which You gave me, to give thanks to Your name for it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:15.395876704Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}